        Identifying dynamical systems characterized by nonlinear parameters presents significant challenges in deriving mathematical models that enhance understanding of physics. Traditional methods, such as Sparse Identification of Nonlinear Dynamics (SINDy) and symbolic regression, can extract governing equations from observational data; however, they also come with distinct advantages and disadvantages&hellip;
        <a class="is-size-7" style="white-space: nowrap;" onclick="document.getElementById('2410.16528v3-abstract-full').style.display = 'inline'; document.getElementById('2410.16528v3-abstract-short').style.display = 'none';">&#9661; More</a>
